858
00:39:30,760 --> 00:39:31,550
I'm sorry.

859
00:39:31,710 --> 00:39:32,650
I didn't know.

860
00:39:33,920 --> 00:39:35,500
You should have known.

861
00:39:42,090 --> 00:39:42,960
So,

862
00:39:43,460 --> 00:39:46,400
the campus card in your wallet

863
00:39:46,940 --> 00:39:48,340
belonged to Jiang Yuan?

864
00:39:53,170 --> 00:39:53,780
Yeah.

865
00:39:56,460 --> 00:39:57,550
Jiang Yuan and I

866
00:39:58,920 --> 00:40:00,380
grew up together.

867
00:40:01,400 --> 00:40:03,260
I was very naughty when I was a kid.

868
00:40:03,650 --> 00:40:05,050
Whenever I got into trouble,

869
00:40:05,050 --> 00:40:06,450
he always took the blame.

870
00:40:06,920 --> 00:40:07,710
When I fought with

871
00:40:07,710 --> 00:40:08,840
the kids in the yard,

872
00:40:09,550 --> 00:40:10,900
he would help me fight.

873
00:40:13,150 --> 00:40:15,080
Later, we went to college together

874
00:40:15,860 --> 00:40:17,060
and founded the team.

875
00:40:18,690 --> 00:40:21,290
The team's performance
got better and better.

876
00:40:21,460 --> 00:40:25,090
We were busy securing postgraduate recommendations
and publishing papers.

877
00:40:25,090 --> 00:40:26,290
But during that time,

878
00:40:29,590 --> 00:40:31,530
Yuan became quieter and quieter.

879
00:40:35,300 --> 00:40:36,400
Later, I found out

880
00:40:37,800 --> 00:40:38,920
he had depression.

881
00:40:40,710 --> 00:40:41,610
Depression?

882
00:40:43,230 --> 00:40:44,040
Why?

883
00:40:45,550 --> 00:40:46,690
At first, I thought

884
00:40:46,710 --> 00:40:48,370
it was the pressure of his PhD.

885
00:40:49,610 --> 00:40:51,090
As long as he finished his thesis

886
00:40:51,090 --> 00:40:52,220
and got his diploma,

887
00:40:53,320 --> 00:40:54,650
his mood would improve.

888
00:40:56,190 --> 00:40:57,210
I even sent him a lot of

889
00:40:57,210 --> 00:40:59,470
my modeling work and experimental data.

890
00:41:02,550 --> 00:41:03,610
But I didn't expect

891
00:41:06,820 --> 00:41:07,610
that these things only caused

892
00:41:07,610 --> 00:41:09,210
his stress to mount further.

893
00:41:11,020 --> 00:41:11,880
His depression

894
00:41:13,690 --> 00:41:14,900
also got worse.

895
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:25,980
The doctor advised him to take
a break from his studies at the time.

896
00:41:27,400 --> 00:41:28,510
Yuan didn't agree.

897
00:41:29,320 --> 00:41:31,320
His parents couldn't persuade him.

898
00:41:32,000 --> 00:41:33,190
So I promised them.

899
00:41:33,610 --> 00:41:34,420
I said

900
00:41:34,880 --> 00:41:35,860
I would definitely take good care

901
00:41:35,860 --> 00:41:36,980
of him at school

902
00:41:38,290 --> 00:41:38,960
and watch him

903
00:41:38,960 --> 00:41:40,690
take his medication every day.

904
00:41:41,630 --> 00:41:43,830
But I only found out after he passed away

905
00:41:45,300 --> 00:41:46,430
that he had secretly

906
00:41:47,900 --> 00:41:49,420
spit out all those pills.

907
00:41:52,900 --> 00:41:53,500
You...

908
00:41:54,710 --> 00:41:56,170
You can't blame yourself.

909
00:41:56,590 --> 00:41:57,910
It's not your fault.

910
00:42:00,550 --> 00:42:01,960
If it weren't for me,

911
00:42:06,710 --> 00:42:07,460
would he

912
00:42:07,460 --> 00:42:08,820
have suffered less?

913
00:42:13,460 --> 00:42:14,780
Since then,

914
00:42:17,920 --> 00:42:19,580
I've been having nightmares.

915
00:42:21,150 --> 00:42:22,190
I often dreamed

916
00:42:24,190 --> 00:42:26,450
about him jumping off the dorm building.

917
00:42:26,920 --> 00:42:28,650
I dreamed of him saying to me...

918
00:42:30,440 --> 00:42:31,280
"Shize.

919
00:42:34,900 --> 00:42:36,630
Why did I ever have to meet you?"

920
00:42:41,400 --> 00:42:43,190
For a very long time, I felt

921
00:42:43,630 --> 00:42:44,880
extremely guilty.

922
00:42:45,790 --> 00:42:46,900
I always wondered,

923
00:42:48,210 --> 00:42:49,460
if I had

924
00:42:50,760 --> 00:42:52,420
cared a little more about him,

925
00:42:53,760 --> 00:42:54,400
if I had

926
00:42:54,400 --> 00:42:55,800
taken better care of him,

927
00:42:56,280 --> 00:42:56,860
or if

928
00:42:56,860 --> 00:42:57,860
I hadn't stayed in the lab

929
00:42:57,860 --> 00:42:59,210
and had gone back to the dorm
with him instead...

930
00:42:59,210 --> 00:43:00,140
would he have...

931
00:43:02,690 --> 00:43:03,780
Or maybe...

932
00:43:06,780 --> 00:43:08,310
if I weren't in the picture,

933
00:43:11,710 --> 00:43:12,460
would he

934
00:43:17,190 --> 00:43:18,860
still be alive and well now?

935
00:43:23,210 --> 00:43:23,800
Shize.

936
00:43:24,460 --> 00:43:26,190
He was sick.

937
00:43:27,110 --> 00:43:28,420
When people are sick,

938
00:43:28,450 --> 00:43:29,570
they say a lot of things

939
00:43:29,570 --> 00:43:31,050
they can't control.

940
00:43:31,260 --> 00:43:32,960
You were his best friend.

941
00:43:33,860 --> 00:43:35,100
He... When he said those things,

942
00:43:35,100 --> 00:43:36,300
he definitely didn't

943
00:43:36,320 --> 00:43:37,690
mean any of it.

944
00:43:43,090 --> 00:43:45,150
Many people have tried to persuade me

945
00:43:46,690 --> 00:43:47,760
to move on.

946
00:43:50,550 --> 00:43:51,510
But I can't do it.

947
00:43:54,170 --> 00:43:55,770
I can't stop blaming myself.

948
00:44:06,820 --> 00:44:07,510
Lili.

949
00:44:12,570 --> 00:44:13,150
I should have

950
00:44:13,150 --> 00:44:15,150
told you about these a long time ago.

951
00:44:15,690 --> 00:44:17,090
But I never had the courage

952
00:44:17,090 --> 00:44:18,960
to truly face them.

953
00:44:20,090 --> 00:44:20,900
I...

954
00:44:22,460 --> 00:44:23,660
I was also very afraid

955
00:44:27,000 --> 00:44:28,050
of recalling

956
00:44:28,050 --> 00:44:28,980
these memories.

957
00:44:29,360 --> 00:44:31,400
♪ The dusk settles slow ♪

958
00:44:30,960 --> 00:44:31,650
So I kept them

959
00:44:31,420 --> 00:44:34,430
♪ Too faint of heart to follow through ♪

960
00:44:31,650 --> 00:44:32,980
to myself all this time.

961
00:44:36,600 --> 00:44:38,600
♪ It's grown like a habit ♪

962
00:44:37,110 --> 00:44:38,010
Lili,

963
00:44:38,630 --> 00:44:41,630
♪ Awaiting dark clouds to spread ♪

964
00:44:41,500 --> 00:44:42,300
I'm sorry.

965
00:44:43,920 --> 00:44:46,280
♪ Lingering right here ♪

966
00:44:44,150 --> 00:44:45,680
Can you please not blame me?

967
00:44:46,530 --> 00:44:48,040
♪ Who tries to talk me down? ♪

968
00:44:46,650 --> 00:44:49,000
I... I never blamed you.

969
00:44:48,080 --> 00:44:49,910
♪ Who makes excuses now? ♪

970
00:44:49,930 --> 00:44:52,880
♪ Let memories trail in threads ♪

971
00:44:53,540 --> 00:44:56,580
♪ Too shattered to pick up ♪

972
00:44:58,260 --> 00:44:59,420
Actually, you've met him.

973
00:44:58,470 --> 00:45:01,820
♪ Afraid it's too late ♪

974
00:45:01,150 --> 00:45:02,940
I've met Jiang Yuan?

975
00:45:02,030 --> 00:45:05,070
♪ Willingly I wait ♪

976
00:45:05,050 --> 00:45:06,110
Do you remember

977
00:45:05,420 --> 00:45:10,300
♪ To soothe the sorry I said yesterday ♪

978
00:45:06,920 --> 00:45:08,520
when you were in high school,

979
00:45:09,260 --> 00:45:10,510
you went to XUST once

980
00:45:10,890 --> 00:45:12,850
♪ Half a phrase unspoken ♪

981
00:45:11,920 --> 00:45:13,500
and played soccer with a robot?

982
00:45:12,880 --> 00:45:16,130
♪ Always too late ♪

983
00:45:14,710 --> 00:45:16,210
The person who gave you
the soccer ball then

984
00:45:16,160 --> 00:45:18,620
♪ Time freezes still ♪

985
00:45:17,150 --> 00:45:18,150
was Jiang Yuan.

986
00:45:19,160 --> 00:45:21,670
♪ My care burns hot ♪

987
00:45:20,260 --> 00:45:22,710
That... That person?

988
00:45:21,830 --> 00:45:25,240
♪ Hidden from your sight ♪

989
00:45:30,280 --> 00:45:32,030
You've already done very well.

990
00:45:32,820 --> 00:45:33,610
He...

991
00:45:34,340 --> 00:45:35,820
I don't know how to say this,

992
00:45:35,820 --> 00:45:36,570
really.

993
00:45:37,070 --> 00:45:38,800
Even though I only met him once,

994
00:45:39,090 --> 00:45:40,130
in my memory,

995
00:45:40,130 --> 00:45:41,740
he was a very good person.

996
00:45:41,800 --> 00:45:43,900
He was so gentle and kind.

997
00:45:41,970 --> 00:45:45,190
♪ Afraid it's too late ♪

998
00:45:43,900 --> 00:45:45,210
He wouldn't have wanted

999
00:45:45,210 --> 00:45:48,690
♪ For me to keep my promise ♪

1000
00:45:45,230 --> 00:45:46,840
you to live with such guilt.

1001
00:45:48,940 --> 00:45:54,030
♪ Let debts bid farewell to unease ♪

1002
00:45:52,070 --> 00:45:52,840
Shize.

1003
00:45:54,400 --> 00:45:56,400
♪ We drift apart, each on our way ♪

1004
00:45:54,590 --> 00:45:55,590
Is there anything

1005
00:45:56,400 --> 00:45:58,090
I can do for you?

1006
00:45:56,420 --> 00:45:59,590
♪ Maybe someday ♪

1007
00:45:59,620 --> 00:46:02,460
♪ Longing finds its way ♪

1008
00:46:02,540 --> 00:46:09,130
♪ I hope you write
the ending of our tale ♪

1009
00:46:09,200 --> 00:46:19,880
♪ I hope you write
the ending of our tale ♪

1010
00:46:20,170 --> 00:46:21,230
Stay by my side.
